BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:73234b355933e21f@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20261021T155235Z
DTSTART:20270112T230000Z
DTEND:20270113T000000Z
SUMMARY:An herbalist's perspective on  Autoimmune conditions
LOCATION:Miller-Vincent Room
URL:https://keenenh.libcal.com/event/17724147
CATEGORIES:kids\,Keene Public Library
DESCRIPTION:Lior Sadeh\, from Three Fold Herbal Healing presents An herbal
 ist’s perspective on  Autoimmune conditions\n\nAutoimmune conditions occ
 ur when the immune system mistakenly attacks the body’s own tissues. Wit
 h more than 80 recognized autoimmune conditions\, they range from organ sp
 ecific disorders\, such as Hashimoto’s thyroiditis\, to systemic disease
 s\, such as lupus. Living with flare-ups\, joint pain\, and fatigue can fe
 el overwhelming\, but research suggests that factors such as gut health\, 
 nutrition\, stress management\, and targeted nutrients may help support im
 mune balance and overall well-being.\n\nThis workshop translates complex m
 edical science into clear\, practical strategies you can incorporate into 
 everyday life. You’ll explore how the gut lining functions\, how food ch
 oices can influence inflammation\, and how simple daily habits can support
  your health and help you feel your best. Registration is appreciated. \n\
 nLior Sadeh\, is a clinical herbalist who weaves modern\, evidence-based k
 nowledge with traditional Western herbalism. As a "retired" farmer with ov
 er a decade of experience in herb growing and medicine-making\, she has de
 veloped an intimate relationship with many of the herbs she uses in her pr
 actice.\n\nLior practices root cause herbalism. One phrase that you will o
 ften hear her say is\, "It's Not what you take\; it's what you Do."\n\nThr
 ough her workshops she hopes you gain a better understanding your body's l
 anguage\, so you can:\n\n\n	Advocate for your health by asking the right q
 uestions when you visit your PCP\n	Make small steps toward a lifestyle bet
 ter suited for your body while being supported every step of the way.\nSou
 rce: Keene Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6577b073956f9906@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20261021T155235Z
DTSTART:20270210T170000Z
DTEND:20270210T220000Z
SUMMARY:American Red Cross Blood Drive
LOCATION:Heberton Hall
URL:https://keenenh.libcal.com/event/17124293
CATEGORIES:kids\,Keene Public Library
DESCRIPTION:Join KPL and the Red Cross for a summer blood drive! Consider 
 donating blood to help others in need. Please call 1-800-RED CROSS (1-800-
 733-2767) or visit RedCrossBlood.org and enter: KEENE to schedule an appoi
 ntment. Maximize your blood donation and help more patients. If you are an
  eligible type O\, B - or A - donor\, consider making a Power Red donation
 . Red blood cells are the most commonly transfused blood component. Stream
 line your donation experience and save up to 15 minutes by visiting RedCro
 ssBlood.org/RapidPass to complete your pre-donation reading and health his
 tory questions on the day of your appointment.\nSource: Keene Public Libra
 ry
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:455957dc350b5132@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20261021T155235Z
DTSTART:20270309T230000Z
DTEND:20270310T000000Z
SUMMARY:Histamine Unlocked: Seasonal Allergies\, Intolerances\, and Mast C
 ells Made Simple
LOCATION:Miller-Vincent Room
URL:https://keenenh.libcal.com/event/17724148
CATEGORIES:kids\,Keene Public Library
DESCRIPTION:Lior Sadeh of Three Fold Herbal Healing presents: \n\nHistamin
 e Unlocked: Seasonal Allergies\, Intolerances\, and Mast Cells Made Simple
 \n\nWhy does seasonal pollen make us sneeze\, and why do some people react
  to everyday foods\, temperature changes\, or stress? Join us at the libra
 ry for an engaging\, easy to understand presentation on histamine and the 
 immune cells that regulate its release.\n\nWe’ll break down complex immu
 ne processes to explore histamine’s role in seasonal allergies\, what ca
 n contribute to histamine intolerance\, and how Mast Cell Activation Syndr
 ome (MCAS) affects the body. You’ll leave with a clearer understanding o
 f how your immune system works\, along with practical strategies to help m
 anage histamine related symptoms\, including seasonal allergies\, and supp
 ort overall well-being. Registration is Required.\n\nLior Sadeh\, is a cli
 nical herbalist who weaves modern\, evidence-based knowledge with traditio
 nal Western herbalism. As a "retired" farmer with over a decade of experie
 nce in herb growing and medicine-making\, she has developed an intimate re
 lationship with many of the herbs she uses in her practice.\n\nLior practi
 ces root cause herbalism. One phrase that you will often hear her say is\,
  "It's Not what you take\; it's what you Do."\n\nThrough her workshops she
  hopes you gain a better understanding your body's language\, so you can:\
 n\n\n	Advocate for your health by asking the right questions when you visi
 t your PCP\n	Make small steps toward a lifestyle better suited for your bo
 dy while being supported every step of the way.\nSource: Keene Public Libr
 ary
END:VEVENT
