SUMMARY:Filipino Storytime
LOCATION:Meeting Room A – Community Meeting Room\, 224 Main Street\, Bra
 ttleboro\, VT\, 05301\, United States
URL:https://brookslibraryvt.org/event/filipino-storytime-4/
CATEGORIES:kids\,Brooks Memorial Library
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special bilingual storytime in Filipino and Engl
 ish to celebrate Filipino American Heritage Month! \nAnna Gail Caunca will
  be reading Kalipay and the Tiniest TikTik by Christina Newhard\, teaching
  us a few words in Tagalog and Cebuano\, and making a craft.  \nThis is a 
 free event. All ages are welcome!\nSource: Brooks Memorial Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d05547a201248472@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20261021T155235Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261024T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261024T120000
SUMMARY:Talking About Tech: AI: The Good\, the Bad\, and the Everyday
LOCATION:Meeting Room D – Quiet Reading Room\, 224 Main Street\, Brattle
 boro\, VT\, 05301\, United States
URL:https://brookslibraryvt.org/event/talking-about-tech-2/
CATEGORIES:kids\,Brooks Memorial Library
DESCRIPTION:Illustration AI-generated with Google Gemini.  Can you spot t
 he signs? \nIn September\, Bob Jude Ferrante led us through some of the hi
 story of Artificial Intelligence\, explained some of the buzzwords and a b
 it about how AI works. This month\, we’ll have an open discussion about 
 AI. Bring your questions\, your observations\, and your honest thoughts. \
 nWe’ll talk through the big concerns—like the impact on jobs\, the env
 ironment\, creativity\, and safety—as well as practical tips\, everyday 
 uses\, and hopes for where technology is heading \nHow has AI changed how 
 we search the internet? What does that mean about whether we can trust the
  information we do find? What about the ethics of training AI on huge amou
 nts of copyrighted books\, music\, images? \nHave you used it to draft an 
 email for you? Had a conversation with someone speaking in another languag
 e? Had an app tell you what song’s stuck in your head by hearing you hum
  a few lines? \nWhether you use AI tools daily\, feel skeptical\, are deep
 ly concerned\, or are just curious to learn what others think\, all perspe
 ctives and experience levels are welcome.\nSource: Brooks Memorial Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:84fd98b6115a69dc@kidcal
