DTSTAMP:20261021T155235Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261103T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261103T200000
SUMMARY:Spirit Chasers: A 30 Year Passion with the Human Form in Nature
LOCATION:Main Reading Room
URL:https://brookslibraryvt.org/event/spirit-chasers-a-30-year-passion-wit
 h-the-human-form-in-nature/
CATEGORIES:kids\,Brooks Memorial Library
DESCRIPTION:All are welcome to this book launch with authors Don Carson an
 d Susan Murphy\, as part of the Vermont Circus Festival. \nThe Vermont Cir
 cus Festival is hosting a literary event launching the newly published boo
 k by one of the original trapeze dancers Susan Murphy and her husband phot
 ographer Don Carson. \nSpirit Chasers is a visually stunning book of photo
 graphy and word. For over three decades\, Don and Susan traveled together 
 across the deserts\, canyons\, rivers\, and redwood forests of the America
 n West. What emerged from these journeys is a rare collaboration of moveme
 nt and stillness\, earth and spirit\, tangible presence and ephemeral phot
 ographic imagery. \nDon’s in-camera photography\, crafted before the age
  of digital editing\, is inventive\, surprising\, and often quietly humoro
 us. Susan\, a pioneer in aerial dance\, brings her practice into wild land
  scapes\, partnering with rock\, water\, trees\, and light. With Susan’s
  journal reflections accompanying Don’s photographs\, this husband and w
 ife team takes us deeply into the awe-inspiring images of these wild natur
 al places.  doncarsonphoto.com/spirit-chasers/\; necenterforcircusarts.or
 g/\nSource: Brooks Memorial Library
END:VEVENT
