SUMMARY:Fall Puzzle Race and Swap
URL:https://putneylibrary.org/event/fall-puzzle-race-and-swap/
CATEGORIES:kids\,Putney Public Library
DESCRIPTION:Fall Puzzle Race and Swap\nRegister by October 19th!\nPuzzle R
 ace on Saturday\, October 24th at 1pm\nPuzzle Swap 10am-2pm \nCan you comp
 lete a jigsaw puzzle faster than your friends and neighbors? Putney Public
  Library will be hosting our Puzzle Race on Saturday\, October 24th at 1pm
 . Register a team of 3-5 puzzlers (OR as an individual willing to join an 
 Extra Pieces team) at https://forms.gle/EXRoQtKyzYW8SkvH7 by \nMonday\, Oc
 tober 19th for a friendly competition to see who can complete a 500 piece 
 puzzle the fastest. Each team will receive the same puzzle. The team that 
 finishes first wins bragging rights! \nThere will also be a Puzzle Swap du
 ring open hours 10am-1pm that Saturday and through the Puzzle Race. Bring 
 a puzzle\, take a puzzle (or three) from the puzzle table.\nSource: Putney
  Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:64ed20412b5673a9@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20261021T155235Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261026T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261026T200000
SUMMARY:Journey Through Pakistan with Umama: Beyond the Headlines and Into
  Daily Life
URL:https://putneylibrary.org/event/journey-through-pakistan-with-umama-be
 yond-the-headlines-and-into-daily-life/
CATEGORIES:kids\,Putney Public Library
DESCRIPTION:Journey Through Pakistan with Umama: Beyond the Headlines and 
 Into Daily Life \nMonday\, October 26th at 6:30pm \nJoin Putney resident U
 mama Ahmed for a presentation about her country of origin\, Pakistan! Thro
 ugh photos and stories\, Umama will take you on a colorful journey through
  Pakistan\, its people\, places\, food\, traditions\, history\, and breath
 taking landscapes\, and explore how the stories and media representations 
 shape the way we see a country. \nUmama Ahmed is an immigrant from Pakista
 n who moved to Vermont in 2025 and has been lucky enough to be both loved 
 by and fall in love with Putney. She has a bachelor’s degree in Literatu
 re from Pakistan and is currently pursuing a Master’s in Business Analyt
 ics at UMass Amherst. \nPutney Public Library is located at 55 Main St in 
 Putney\, VT. This event is free and open to the public.\nSource: Putney Pu
 blic Library
END:VEVENT
